1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
WebMCP makes a website callable by agents. WorkHub Goal Room makes each call state-aware, authority-checked, evidence-bound, and owner-controlled.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A callable action is not automatically a legal action. An agent can act on stale state, bind evidence to the wrong Plan, or mistake PASS for acceptance.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Goal Room registers exactly five WebMCP tools. Every consequential call enters the same authority kernel and is revalidated against the current legal frontier.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Owner confirmation, verifier authorship, final acceptance, and external effects are intentionally not WebMCP tools.

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The agent proposed Plan v1, but work is blocked until the owner confirms it. Then the agent may claim only an admitted step.

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The agent submits exact candidate bytes and their SHA-256 digest. Candidate v1 enters deterministic verification and fails.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The original evidence and FAIL receipt remain immutable. The agent submits corrected Candidate v2.

8
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:54,000
The internal verifier records PASS. PASS does not accept the Goal; it only permits the agent to request completion for this exact candidate.

9
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The frontier moves to the owner. The agent and verifier are blocked. Only the owner can accept the exact verified candidate.

10
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:30,000
After acceptance, every lifecycle stage is complete and there is no further governed action.

11
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Humans and agents can share one state machine without sharing one authority level.
